---
import catalog from '../../data/catalog.json';
import { filterCatalog, TESTED_VERSION } from '../lib/catalog.mjs';
import DownloadRow from '../components/DownloadRow.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const entries = filterCatalog(catalog.entries, { platform: 'windows' });
const versions = new Set(catalog.entries.map(entry => entry.version)).size;
const repository = 'https://github.com/RobyRew/BlockTheSpot-Installer';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="Browse Spotify desktop installers for Windows, macOS and Linux. Search versions, filter architectures, and choose official Spotify or clearly labeled mirror downloads." />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f8f5" />
    <title>Spotify version library · BlockTheSpot</title>
    <link rel="icon" href={`${base}/favicon.svg`} type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={`${Astro.site}${base.slice(1)}/`} />
    <script is:inline>try { document.documentElement.dataset.theme = localStorage.getItem('catalog-theme') || 'light'; } catch {}</script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#catalog">Skip to version library</a>
    <header class="header">
      <a class="brand" href={`${base}/`}><img src={`${base}/favicon.svg`} width="34" height="34" alt="" /><span>BlockTheSpot<span class="brand-divider">/</span><span class="brand-section">Downloads</span></span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a class="active" href="#catalog">Version library</a><a href="#installer">Installer</a><a href={repository}>GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><button id="theme-toggle" class="icon-button" aria-label="Switch color theme" title="Switch color theme">◐</button></nav>
    </header>
    <main>
      <section class="intro" aria-labelledby="page-title">
        <div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> THE DESKTOP COLLECTION</p><h1 id="page-title">Your Spotify.<br /><span>Your version.</span></h1><p class="intro-copy">Find the desktop installer you need. Every platform, every architecture, all in one searchable library.</p></div>
        <div class="collection-summary"><div class="summary-mark" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="metrics"><div><strong>{versions}</strong><span>versions indexed</span></div><div><strong>3</strong><span>desktop platforms</span></div></div><p>Catalog updated <time datetime={catalog.updatedAt}>{new Date(catalog.updatedAt).toISOString().slice(0, 10)}</time><br /><span>Checks for new versions every 6 hours</span></p></div>
      </section>

      <section class="quick-downloads" aria-label="Quick downloads">
        <article class="installer-card" id="installer">
          <div class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">↓</div><div class="quick-copy"><div class="card-title">BlockTheSpot Installer <span class="badge" id="app-version">v0.4.0</span></div><p>Native Windows app. One guided install.</p><a class="compatibility" href={`${base}/?q=${TESTED_VERSION}&architecture=x64#catalog`}>Tested with Spotify {TESTED_VERSION}</a></div><a class="button primary" href={`${repository}/releases/latest/download/BlockTheSpotInstaller.exe`}>Get installer <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="official-card"><span class="eyebrow">STRAIGHT FROM SPOTIFY</span><h2>Just need the latest?</h2><div class="official-links"><a data-official-download href="https://download.scdn.co/SpotifyFullSetupX64.exe">Windows x64 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a data-official-download href="https://download.scdn.co/Spotify.dmg">Mac Intel <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a data-official-download href="https://download.scdn.co/SpotifyARM64.dmg">Mac Apple silicon <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="https://www.spotify.com/download/linux/">Linux <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><p>Current official builds. BTS compatibility may vary.</p></article>
      </section>

      <section class="library" id="catalog" aria-labelledby="library-title" data-api={`${base}/api/v1/catalog.json`}>
        <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">FIND YOUR BUILD</p><h2 id="library-title">Version library <span class="total-count">{catalog.entries.length.toLocaleString('en-US')} installers</span></h2></div><a class="text-link" href={`${base}/api/v1/catalog.json`}>JSON feed <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        <div class="filter-panel">
          <div class="filter-top"><div class="platform-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Platform"><button data-platform="all" aria-pressed="false">All platforms</button><button data-platform="windows" aria-pressed="true"><span aria-hidden="true">⊞</span> Windows</button><button data-platform="macos" aria-pressed="false">macOS</button><button data-platform="linux" aria-pressed="false">Linux</button></div><label class="search"><span aria-hidden="true">⌕</span><input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Search a version or build…" aria-label="Search Spotify versions" autocomplete="off" /><kbd>/</kbd></label></div>
          <div class="filter-bottom"><label>Architecture<select id="architecture"><option value="all">All architectures</option><option value="x64">x64 / Intel</option><option value="arm64">ARM64 / Apple silicon</option><option value="x86">x86 (32-bit)</option></select></label><label>Download source<select id="source"><option value="all">All sources</option><option value="official">Official Spotify only</option><option value="mirror">LoadSpot mirrors</option></select></label><label class="sort-filter">Sort by<select id="sort"><option value="newest">Newest first</option><option value="oldest">Oldest first</option></select></label><button id="reset" class="reset-button">Reset filters</button></div>
        </div>
        <div class="results-heading"><p id="result-count" role="status" aria-live="polite">{entries.length} installers for Windows</p><span><span class="tiny-dot"></span> BTS tested version is marked</span></div>
        <p class="catalog-notice">Official links go to Spotify’s servers. Mirrors are hosted by LoadSpot. Older official CDN links may have expired; select a mirror if Spotify no longer serves that build. macOS and Linux downloads are Spotify clients only.</p>
        <p id="load-error" class="error" hidden>Could not load the full library. The first results are shown below. <button id="retry">Try again</button></p>
        <noscript><p class="catalog-notice">Enable JavaScript to search all versions, or <a href={`${base}/api/v1/catalog.json`}>download the full JSON catalog</a>. The first 30 Windows results appear below.</p></noscript>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table><caption class="sr-only">Spotify desktop installers</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Version / build</th><th scope="col">Platform</th><th scope="col">Released / size</th><th scope="col">Source</th><th scope="col"><span class="sr-only">Download</span></th></tr></thead><tbody id="results">{entries.slice(0, 30).map(entry => <DownloadRow entry={entry} />)}</tbody></table><div id="empty" class="empty-state" hidden><span aria-hidden="true">⌕</span><h3>No builds match these filters</h3><p>Try a shorter version number or a different architecture.</p><button id="empty-reset" class="button">Clear filters</button></div></div>
        <div class="pagination"><span id="page-label">Showing 1–30 of {entries.length}</span><div><button id="previous" disabled aria-label="Previous page">← Previous</button><button id="next" disabled aria-label="Next page">Next →</button></div></div>
      </section>
      <section class="about-grid" aria-label="About this library"><article><span class="note-number">01 / SOURCES</span><h3>Know where it comes from.</h3><p>Current builds from <a href="https://github.com/LoaderSpot/table">LoadSpot’s maintained catalog</a>, historical Spotify CDN links from <a href="https://github.com/LoaderSpot/LoaderSpot">LoaderSpot</a>, and Linux packages from Spotify’s repository. Files are downloaded from the labeled source.</p></article><article><span class="note-number">02 / COMPATIBILITY</span><h3>A catalog is not a compatibility list.</h3><p>BlockTheSpot Installer defaults to <strong>{TESTED_VERSION}</strong> on Windows x64. Other versions and platforms are here for browsing; newer builds require an explicit choice in the installer.</p></article><article><span class="note-number">03 / ALWAYS AVAILABLE</span><h3>A small, fast feed.</h3><p>The library is generated with Astro and served by GitHub Pages. The installer reads a <a href={`${base}/api/v1/windows-x64.json`}>compact Windows feed</a> and can fall back to the upstream catalog when needed.</p></article></section>
    </main>
    <footer><a class="footer-brand" href={repository}>BlockTheSpot <span>Open source, made for your desktop.</span></a><p>Not affiliated with Spotify. Support artists with <a href="https://www.spotify.com/premium/">Spotify Premium</a>.</p><a href={`${repository}/issues`}>Report an issue ↗</a></footer>
    <script src="../lib/browser.mjs"></script>
  </body>
</html>
